From cb60f9c33cff9897f49d110ed22c68829bb60da9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tamir Duberstein <tamird@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:02:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [ty] Preserve literals in loop unpacking

Destructuring an immediately consumed list in a loop widened literal
values, while iteration with a single target preserved them. This also
rejected literal arguments passed from destructured comprehensions.

Share the existing precise iterable-element inference with unpacking and
use it for synchronous list displays. Keep the normal iteration fallback
for empty and unknown-length inputs, and for stored mutable containers.
